The failing cleanup regression exposed a real cancellation inheritance bug: an upload timeout’s canceled child was entering channel cleanup and closing the shared TCP bridge. Cleanup now runs in a fresh owned actor task, so the exec/upload channel is reset while subsequent siblings remain usable. The new rejected-open test also verifies operation scope and explicit unsupported RFC reason reporting.
