 ## 2026-08-10
 
+### 1858 — libssh2 adapter closes review round 4 cancellation and cleanup gaps (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
+- ROOT CAUSE: Long-lived reads reused the write-credit deadline; the authentication timeout raced a waiter that still joined an independently owned signer; rekey and keepalive deadlines began only after the shared session gate; and canceled upload cleanup inherited task cancellation, causing its cleanup progress handler to close the shared TCP bridge.
+- REWORK: Reads now wait without an implicit idle deadline while retaining operation-scoped cancellation. Socket and signer completion waiters let callers detach promptly, while teardown cancels and joins owned work. Rekey uses the earlier of the caller-visible explicit deadline and `SSHRekeyPolicy.timeout` before gate admission; one keepalive may queue behind KEX. EOF takes the per-channel write gate after accepted writes, and uncertain EOF/exec/upload failures run bounded uncancelled channel reset while siblings survive.
+- ERROR SHAPE: Engine channel-open rejection is operation-scoped with explicit `unsupported` RFC reason evidence. EOF and exec-exit failures carry channel scope; upload timeout carries operation scope; connection errors remain lane-scoped and fatal. No deferred semantic is fabricated.
+- VERIFICATION: `swift test --filter LibSSH2` passes 27 tests/3 suites; `make validate-core` passes 361 tests/31 suites plus build and boundary checks; strict Swift format and diff checks pass; `make validate-libssh2`, source tamper gates, and the dual-architecture extension-safe macOS provider/harness matrix all exit 0. Logs use the task-scoped `*-05.log` names under `.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/`.
+
 ### 1824 — libssh2 adapter preserves operation scope and nonblocking argument identity (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
 - ROOT CAUSE: Channel read/write timeout cancellation shut down the shared socket bridge; channel opens rejected `rekeying` before entering the session gate and started their deadline only after gate admission; each rekey caller owned the connection-global KEX; and concurrent writes could resume libssh2's single per-channel write state with a different payload after `EAGAIN`. Credential results were checked against factory capabilities but not the caller-provided allowlist.
 - REWORK: Socket-service cancellation now retires only its independently cancellable readiness operation. Channel opens may queue behind rekey under their original bounded deadline. One bounded shared rekey flight coalesces trigger reasons and lets a canceled caller detach while KEX continues. Per-channel FIFO gates retain exact write arguments across `EAGAIN`, with queued bytes still reserved against the caller cap. Returned credential algorithms must belong to both adapter capabilities and the request allowlist.
